WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.541 --> 00:00:29.750


2
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:34.833
<b>In the previous few verses, Arjuna was</b>
<b>expressing his fear of the destruction of a lineage,</b>

3
00:00:34.833 --> 00:00:37.083
<b>and now here he says,</b>

4
00:00:37.083 --> 00:00:38.291
<b>O Janardana,</b>

5
00:00:38.291 --> 00:00:43.583
<b>those whose family dharma has been destroyed,</b>
<b>such men dwell in hell.</b>

6
00:00:43.583 --> 00:00:47.916
<b>This is what I have heard through</b>
<b>the guru-disciple tradition.</b>

7
00:00:48.416 --> 00:00:52.583


8
00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:56.958
<b>Despite being such a great warrior</b>
<b>and a great scholar, Arjuna has</b>

9
00:00:56.958 --> 00:00:58.875
<b>no trace of arrogance.</b>

10
00:00:58.875 --> 00:00:59.750
<b>Here too,</b>

11
00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:02.250
<b>he is portraying himself as small.</b>

12
00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:03.833
<b>It's as if he is saying,</b>

13
00:01:03.833 --> 00:01:05.708
<b>"I am not so knowledgeable</b>

14
00:01:05.708 --> 00:01:08.500
<b>that I can say all these things from my own mind.</b>

15
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:13.458
<b>All this has been taught to me,</b>
<b>the disciple, by my revered gurus."</b>

16
00:01:14.125 --> 00:01:18.291


17
00:01:18.291 --> 00:01:20.083
<b>On one hand, there's Arjuna,</b>

18
00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:25.208
<b>who could grasp victory in his fist if he wished,</b>

19
00:01:25.208 --> 00:01:28.666
<b>yet he contemplates,</b>

20
00:01:28.666 --> 00:01:31.875
<b>ponders over right and wrong,</b>

21
00:01:31.875 --> 00:01:33.791
<b>dharma,</b>

22
00:01:33.791 --> 00:01:36.583
<b>and lineage.</b>

23
00:01:36.583 --> 00:01:39.541
<b>There's no conceit in his mind.</b>

24
00:01:39.541 --> 00:01:42.000
<b>And on the other hand, there's Duryodhana,</b>

25
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.166
<b>filled with arrogance,</b>

26
00:01:44.166 --> 00:01:47.625
<b>eager to slay his own,</b>

27
00:01:47.625 --> 00:01:50.875
<b>heeding neither Grandsire Bhishma</b>

28
00:01:50.875 --> 00:01:53.166
<b>nor Guru Drona.</b>

29
00:01:53.166 --> 00:01:59.000
<b>Heeding only his own obstinacy.</b>

30
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.541
<b>Yes,</b>

31
00:02:00.541 --> 00:02:05.208
<b>it's essential to be self-reliant and</b>
<b>make one's own decisions,</b>

32
00:02:05.208 --> 00:02:06.625
<b>but</b>

33
00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:08.291
<b>self-reliance</b>

34
00:02:08.291 --> 00:02:11.166
<b>begins to take the form of ego</b>

35
00:02:11.166 --> 00:02:13.291
<b>when one thinks</b>

36
00:02:13.291 --> 00:02:16.291
<b>they don't need anyone,</b>

37
00:02:16.291 --> 00:02:20.833
<b>that no one can teach them.</b>

38
00:02:20.833 --> 00:02:24.666
<b>Making one's own decisions is necessary,</b>

39
00:02:24.666 --> 00:02:25.666
<b>but </b>

40
00:02:25.666 --> 00:02:29.708
<b>considering others worthless,</b>

41
00:02:29.708 --> 00:02:34.000
<b>that is conceit.</b>

42
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.375
<b>In personal life, both have importance</b>

43
00:02:37.375 --> 00:02:39.583
<b>to keep learning on one's own</b>

44
00:02:39.583 --> 00:02:40.208
<b>and</b>

45
00:02:40.208 --> 00:02:46.458
<b>to seek the opinion of those more</b>
<b>experienced than oneself, of gurus. </b>

46
00:02:46.458 --> 00:02:48.333
<b>It is said</b>

47
00:02:48.333 --> 00:02:49.875
<b>that a person</b>

48
00:02:49.875 --> 00:02:52.875
<b>who considers only himself as his guru</b>

49
00:02:52.875 --> 00:02:57.166
<b>probably has only one disciple,</b>

50
00:02:57.166 --> 00:03:01.208
<b>and even he might be a fool.</b>

51
00:03:01.208 --> 00:03:07.125
<b>Don't become Duryodhana</b>
<b>thinking you don't need anyone,</b>

52
00:03:07.125 --> 00:03:09.625
<b>don't be foolish.</b>

53
00:03:09.625 --> 00:03:10.708
<b>Think</b>

54
00:03:10.708 --> 00:03:12.250
<b>for yourself</b>

55
00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:13.625
<b>Take lessons</b>

56
00:03:13.625 --> 00:03:16.083
<b>from the past</b>

57
00:03:16.083 --> 00:03:18.458
<b>Take opinions and learn</b>

58
00:03:18.458 --> 00:03:20.000
<b>from gurus,</b>

59
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.541
<b>from experienced people.</b>

60
00:03:22.541 --> 00:03:24.708
<b>And then make a decision.</b>

61
00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:29.666


62
00:03:29.666 --> 00:03:33.583
<b>Although Arjuna's thoughts</b>
<b>are entangled at this moment,</b>

63
00:03:33.583 --> 00:03:35.708
<b>he is in a dilemma,</b>

64
00:03:35.708 --> 00:03:36.916
<b>yet</b>

65
00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:41.375
<b>you must have noticed</b>

66
00:03:41.375 --> 00:03:46.291
<b>that behind each of his thoughts,</b>
<b>behind each of his statements</b>

67
00:03:46.291 --> 00:03:48.041
<b>he is providing reasonings.</b>

68
00:03:48.041 --> 00:03:49.458
<b>Like, here </b>

69
00:03:49.458 --> 00:03:51.333
<b> he is explaining</b>

70
00:03:51.333 --> 00:03:56.958
<b>how he has learned all this</b>
<b>in the guru-disciple tradition.</b>

71
00:03:56.958 --> 00:03:59.875
<b>This is indeed the mark of good gurus</b>

72
00:03:59.875 --> 00:04:03.083
<b>and the true knowledge they impart,</b>

73
00:04:03.083 --> 00:04:07.625
<b>that there is not just obstinacy behind</b>
<b>any of Arjuna's statements,</b>

74
00:04:07.625 --> 00:04:13.041
<b>but there is also probable reasoning</b>
<b>behind those statements.</b>

75
00:04:13.041 --> 00:04:16.833
<b>And this is the lesson that elders</b>
<b>in society and family </b>

76
00:04:16.833 --> 00:04:18.000
<b>should take,</b>

77
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.750
<b>it is necessary for them,</b>

78
00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:23.875
<b>that whatever tradition they pass</b>
<b>on to the younger ones, </b>

79
00:04:23.875 --> 00:04:26.333
<b>whatever customs they teach them,</b>

80
00:04:26.333 --> 00:04:29.500
<b>they should also explain</b>
<b>the significance behind it.</b>

81
00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:31.125
<b>Behind every knowledge,</b>

82
00:04:31.125 --> 00:04:36.375
<b>behind every tradition, there is an</b>
<b>inherent significance, a reason. </b>

83
00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:39.291
<b>Only if that is also passed along,</b>

84
00:04:39.291 --> 00:04:42.666
<b>then the true value of those traditions,</b>

85
00:04:42.666 --> 00:04:44.958
<b>the coming generations will understand.</b>

86
00:04:44.958 --> 00:04:50.166
<b>Only then will those traditions</b>
<b>remain alive for many years,</b>

87
00:04:50.166 --> 00:04:52.416
<b>otherwise,</b>

88
00:04:52.416 --> 00:04:57.250
<b>they will be forgotten, considering</b>
<b>them merely an orthodox custom.</b>

89
00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:01.958


90
00:05:01.958 --> 00:05:07.291
<b>Arjun speaks here of the guru-disciple tradition.</b>

91
00:05:07.291 --> 00:05:09.000
<b>He talks about </b>

92
00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:15.708
<b>knowledge passed down from</b>
<b>a guru to disciples, generation after generation.</b>

93
00:05:15.708 --> 00:05:17.291
<b>But</b>

94
00:05:17.291 --> 00:05:21.625
<b>how does this wisdom endure</b>
<b>for so many centuries,</b>

95
00:05:21.625 --> 00:05:24.083
<b>so many generations?</b>

96
00:05:24.083 --> 00:05:26.500
<b>Take this very Gita,</b>

97
00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:32.125
<b>guiding humanity like</b>
<b>a guru for thousands of years.</b>

98
00:05:32.125 --> 00:05:33.500
<b>It's because</b>

99
00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:35.458
<b>someone wrote it,</b>

100
00:05:35.458 --> 00:05:38.625
<b>edited it.</b>

101
00:05:38.625 --> 00:05:41.625
<b>Spoken words have a limited life. </b>

102
00:05:41.625 --> 00:05:42.541
<b>Some words </b>

103
00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:47.041
<b>vanish as they pass from one person to another, </b>

104
00:05:47.041 --> 00:05:50.458
<b>while some change their form.</b>

105
00:05:50.458 --> 00:05:51.250
<b>But</b>

106
00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:54.750
<b>written words neither vanish,</b>

107
00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:57.250
<b>nor do they change their form.</b>

108
00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:01.833
<b>In professional life,</b>
<b>our colleagues keep changing.</b>

109
00:06:01.833 --> 00:06:07.583
<b>In such a situation,</b>
<b>verbal knowledge would quickly disappear.</b>

110
00:06:07.583 --> 00:06:10.041
<b>It's necessary for any organization</b>

111
00:06:10.041 --> 00:06:15.750
<b>to keep a written collection of</b>
<b>important techniques and systems.</b>

112
00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:17.208
<b>And just like that,</b>

113
00:06:17.208 --> 00:06:18.375
<b>it's necessary</b>

114
00:06:18.375 --> 00:06:21.250
<b>for a high-ranking official or a leader</b>

115
00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:25.833
<b>to convey their long-term ideas not just verbally,</b>

116
00:06:25.833 --> 00:06:30.833
<b>but also in written form to people.</b>

117
00:06:30.833 --> 00:06:35.125
<b>So that those ideas don't fade with time.</b>

118
00:06:35.125 --> 00:06:40.333
<b>This too is a far-sighted approach, isn't it?</b>

119
00:06:40.333 --> 00:06:42.208
<b>Think about it.</b>

